      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "With R2 there isn't any issue with \"information leak\" as the only metric or info you get is storage use and how many of each operation.\n\nHowever, with Workers there is \"information leak\". While it would make it more dynamic in terms of data and such, it would also allow for more data collection. Especially if VRChat is actually going to allow for dynamic whitelisted urls (generate urls during runtime based on the url whitelists.\n\nJust something to consider :)\n\nBut with R2, you can make it very dynamic by just uploading a new file with the same name. So things like strings and json is fully supported (Cloudflare even sets the correct headers)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
